# Video Engine Pipeline Standards

## 1. Video Duration & Audio CTA Guarantee (Target: 80 s)

- **Target duration:** 80 seconds (1 m 20 s) — flexible; never hard-cut audio.
- **Narration word count:** 130–140 words (narration body only, ~135 WPM → ~65–70 s).
- **Audio-driven timeline:** `video_render_duration = tts_audio_duration + 1.0 s`  
  The hard 80 s upper cap is **removed** from the voice-driven path so the video never cuts off the CTA.
- **Script trimmer:** Call `_trim_script_to_word_limit(script, max_words=140)` on `_voiceover_script` before TTS — strips `[ACT N]` markers from word count, removes middle filler sentences while preserving the opening hook.

## 2. Sequential CTA Execution (Strict Zero-Overlap Rule)

- **Separate audio blocks:** CTA is NOT embedded in the narration script text.
  - Pass `cta_line=""` to `generate_sequence_voiceover` — no inline CTA instruction.
  - Generate narration TTS → `*_narration.mp3`
  - Generate CTA TTS separately (same voice/model) → `*_cta.mp3`
- **Mandatory 1.0 s gap:** Stitch via `_stitch_audio_sequential(narr, cta, out, silence_s=1.0)`  
  Formula: `total_audio = narration_audio + 1.0 s_silence + cta_audio`
- **Mandatory CTA text (ancient_knowledge):** `"Follow Ancient Knowledge for more hidden mysteries."`
- Stitched file is passed as `voice_audio` to `compile_sequence_reel`; timeline is audio-driven.

## 3. Dynamic Parallax Depth & Aggressive Motion

- **3D depth layering:** Every image prompt MUST specify both foreground elements (dust particles, stone arch, human observer) AND background elements (temple silhouette, starfield, distant horizon) so the camera movement creates visible parallax separation.
- **Motion profiles** (cycle with `act_index % 4`):
  | # | Name | Zoom | Pan mul |
  |---|------|------|---------|
  | 0 | Rapid Push-In | 1.00 → 1.42 | 1.65× |
  | 1 | Wide Pull-Out Reveal | 1.48 → 1.02 | 1.00× reversed |
  | 2 | Sweeping Lateral Parallax | 1.10 → 1.32 | 4.60× |
  | 3 | Overhead Crane Sweep | 1.18 → 1.40 | 2.30× reversed |
- **Base pan amplitudes:** `_PAN_AMP_X = 60 px`, `_PAN_AMP_Y = 42 px`.
- Replace all static slow-zooms with rapid push-ins, wide pull-out reveals, sweeping lateral parallax movements.

## 4. Visual-to-Narration Context Matching

- Entity extraction runs via `_extract_topic_visual_entities(subject)` before each image generation batch.
- Known geo-anchors (Nazca, Pyramids, Baalbek, Easter Island, Stonehenge, Göbekli Tepe, Atlantis, Crystal Skulls, etc.) map to specific camera-perspective directives.
- **No generic stone walls** when specific subjects are named — the prompt must illustrate the exact entity spoken.
- Parallax depth directive appended to every act prompt:
  ```
  DEPTH LAYERS: foreground — [dust particles / stone arch / observer]. 
  Background — [ancient temple / starfield / horizon line].
  ```

## 5. Camera Framing & Safe Zones

- Default all image prompts to **Wide Aerial, High-Altitude, Panoramic, or Environmental** angles.
- Primary subjects must be **centrally framed** to stay clear of social platform UI overlays (Reels/Shorts like/comment buttons).
- **No extreme micro close-ups** that obscure environmental scale or main subject identity.

## 6. Audio Engineering Standards

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Background music volume | `0.70` (≈ −3 dB relative to voiceover) |
| Narration speed | `1.05×` (`_NARRATION_SPEED` in `audio_engine.py`) |
| Sub-bass transition booms | 65 Hz, 400 ms, 0.15 amplitude — synthesised with NumPy at every scene cut |
| Ambient track | ElevenLabs SFX API `/v1/sound-generation`, 20 s loop, `prompt_influence=0.7` |

## 7. Post-FX Toggles (page_config.py per page)

| Flag | Purpose | ancient_knowledge default |
|------|---------|--------------------------|
| `ENABLE_FLICKER` | Torch brightness oscillation | `True` |
| `ENABLE_LIGHT_RAYS` | Volumetric warm-gold beam | `True` |
| `ENABLE_DUST_PARTICLES` | Upward-drifting 55-particle tile | `True` |
| `ENABLE_LIGHT_REFRACTION` | Prismatic crystal glow | `False` (enable per crystal-subject topic) |

## 8. Asset Isolation

- Every reel run creates a new `seq_run_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS/` subfolder inside `subject_assets/`.
- Stale `seq_run_*` directories are deleted via `shutil.rmtree` before generating new act images.
- Act images (acts 2–N) are always written to the isolated run dir, never to the parent `subject_assets/`.

## 9. Image Generation Budget (Dense Scene Sync)

- **Dense target:** ~1 image every 3.5–4.0 s of speech → **12–18 acts** for a 60–80 s reel.
- **Act duration at compile:** `total_audio_duration / n_acts` (audio-driven; never hard-cut VO).
- **Spoken-beat prompts:** Each act image receives the exact ~4 s script snippet being spoken.
- Cap via `REEL_IMAGE_COUNT` (default **18**); `REEL_SECONDS_PER_ACT` defaults to **4.0**.
- Bulk concurrency: `max_workers ≤ 3` to avoid 429 rate-limit storms.
- Override hard duration cap only with explicit `duration_override` on `compile_sequence_reel`.

## 10. 429 / Blinded Act Fallback

- Image provider: on 429 / `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`, sleep **3.0 s** and retry up to **3** times before rotating models.
- Missing act images never raise `FileNotFoundError` — fall back to Act 1 / base / solid placeholder so MoviePy always completes.